WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.299
Bird Box, Netflix's terrifying journey into
a world where you can't trust your eyes, is

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:09.380
packed with intriguing little details that
you'll be thinking about long after the credits

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:09.880
have rolled.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.060
Let's break down those little details, and
what they might mean, as we unpack the movie's

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.560
ending.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.060
One of the most frightening things about Bird
Box is how little it tells us about what's

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.390
really happening to the world, specifically
regarding the mysterious creatures plaguing

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:23.880
humanity.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.460
We know that from a mere glance they can drive
most people to suicide and some people to

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:28.960
madness.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:29.880
But why?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:35.700
Lil Rel Howery's character, Charlie, suggests
that the creatures are demons feeding on souls,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.739
somehow sustaining themselves by devouring
peoples' sanity, but that theory is never

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:45.190
proven, leaving much of the creatures' nature
and what people see when they look at them

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.780
up to the audience's imagination.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.379
Another part of the puzzle the creatures pose
involves where exactly they came from, and

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.160
why they arrived.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.539
We're told the creatures' emergence began
in Eastern Europe before crossing into the

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.149
United States, but that's all we get to go
on.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:05.269
They could be extraterrestrial creatures,
biological weapons, or spiritual demons — all

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:06.939
answers seem equally likely.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.760
"Did you learn all that working at the supermarket?"

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.040
The creatures' unknown motives drive the movie's
mystery, leaving the characters with no clue

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:15.920
what they're up against.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.360
The threat is almost beyond description, which
is where the movie gets most of its horror.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.860
Some questions the characters have to consider
is: Do the creatures reproduce?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.050
Is there a finite number of them, or will
they just keep coming?

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.700
Just how screwed is planet Earth?

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.500
If the protagonists' knew the source of the
monsters, they'd be better equipped to fight

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.000
back.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.960
Instead, all they can rely on is their own
guesswork.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.700
When Malorie and the children - which she
calls “boy” and “girl” - finally arrive

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.970
at Rick's compound down the river, they discover
that it's a school for the blind, complete

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.450
with a bird sanctuary that serves as a kind
of early warning system for the compound's

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.340
sighted residents.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:55.900
It seems to be a secure system, although it
does have some troubling implications for

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.160
the future of humanity.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:01.440
If this is the status quo in the world right
now, and these creatures will never truly

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.499
go away, does that give blind people a genetic
advantage for the future of the human race?

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.480
If Rick and his students survived, other communities
of blind people likely did as well.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.880
The implication is that sightless people are
the only ones who have a chance at thriving

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.360
and living on in a world plagued by these
monsters.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.440
For people who enjoy being able to see the
world, that's a pretty frightening thought.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.660
Unfortunately, the creatures aren't the only
thing that the people in Bird Box have to

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.160
worry about.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.480
There's also the creatures' human acolytes,
who are all bent on exposing everyone to the

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.240
creatures that they can.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.800
Depending on who you talk to, these people
were either already insane when they saw the

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.380
creatures or were driven insane by contact
with them, but in the wake of this contact

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.540
they remain alive and very dangerous.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.000
They're not insane in the sense that they
are incapable of rational behavior.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.580
They can give the appearance of being reasonable,
carry on conversations, and deceive people,

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.280
implying something more nuanced than mere
madness.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.940
If these people are so convinced that everyone
should see the creatures, it stands to reason

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:04.510
that they would choose to reproduce and show
their children as well, potentially raising

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.620
a whole generation of people who find the
creatures "beautiful."

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:14.260
"Look at this"
"Isn't it beautiful?"

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.500
It could all set up a strange future society
in which humanity is divided into two very

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.910
different sides — one trying their hardest
not to look at the creatures, and another

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.540
trying to expose them to the world.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.020
Rick's compound is a school for the blind,
meaning the majority of the people there when

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:34.370
the outbreak began were people who simply
couldn't be influenced by the creatures' strange

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.580
ability to drive people who see them mad.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.060
It's a clever plot development, and it makes
sense in the context of what we know about

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.440
the creatures, but what about the other ways
the creatures can influence humans?

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:49.060
We see during the grocery store run that they're
able to rock the car, which means they can

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:53.490
affect the world in a physical way, and even
when Malorie isn't looking at them, they're

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.900
able to get inside her head and tempt her
with the voices of dead people.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.720
Can they do the same to the blind?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.520
Do they get stronger as they influence more
people?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.900
Are the blind people truly safe in this world,
or can the creatures ultimately find a way

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.770
to influence them too?

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:08.760
Only time will tell.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:14.020
The bird box of the film's title refers in
a literal sense to the cardboard box Malorie

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:18.590
uses to store her birds for the journey down
the river, using the sensitive little birdies

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.900
as an alarm system for when the creatures
or their followers are near.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:27.260
In a metaphorical sense, though, the bird
box can be seen as Malorie's own heart, tensed

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.240
up and locked away while she simply tries
to survive the horrors of her life.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.660
When they finally arrive at the school for
the blind, one of Malorie's first acts of

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:39.920
relief and comfort is to open the box and
release the birds to "be with their friends,"

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.570
and shortly after that she finally softens
with her children, giving them real names

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.060
as a sign that they're now about to live a
better life.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.860
Throughout the film we see Malorie's growth
as a leader, as a mother, and as a survivor,

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.840
and now she's found a place where she doesn't
have to be so harsh all the time as a means

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.840
of staying alive.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.630
Will that strong sense of leadership continue
to be with her in times of crisis, or will

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.380
she continue to soften, and get her humanity
back?

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.460
More likely, she'll just have to find a balance
as she works for a new way forward with her

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.440
fellow survivors.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.620
The ending may be happy enough for her and
her children, but as for the fate of the rest

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:15.120
of the world?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.280
Well it really just doesn't look good.

